Feature: Standardize delivery_dt in f_order table to Decimal (38,0) in yyyymmdd format

  Background:
    Given the SQL script is located at "/Workspace/stg/scripts/f_order.sql"
    And the Unity Catalog is set to "purgo_databricks"
    And the Schema is "purgo_playground"

  Scenario: Validate all delivery_dt values are Decimal (38,0) and in yyyymmdd format
    When the SQL validation is executed
    Then all delivery_dt values should be of type Decimal(38,0)
    And all delivery_dt values should match the format "yyyymmdd"

  Scenario Outline: Validate specific delivery_dt values
    Given a delivery_dt value of "<delivery_dt>"
    When the SQL validation is performed
    Then the validation result should be "<expected_result>"
    And the message should be "<message>"

    Examples:
      | delivery_dt | expected_result | message                         |
      | 20240910    | Pass            | Valid Decimal (38,0) yyyymmdd    |
      | 2024-09-10  | Fail            | Invalid format and datatype      |
      | 2024091A    | Fail            | Non-numeric characters           |
      | 202409      | Fail            | Incorrect length                  |

  Scenario: Log errors for invalid delivery_dt values
    When invalid delivery_dt values are detected
    Then an error should be logged with the message "Invalid delivery_dt format or datatype"

  Scenario: Reject records with non-conforming delivery_dt
    When processing records in f_order table
    Then records with invalid delivery_dt should be rejected
    And an error should be raised for each rejected record
